\begin{frame}{Race in sociolinguistics}
  Present in work since the beginnings of the field
  \begin{enumerate}
    \item The speech of marginalized groups is structured and rule-bound \smallcite{labov_social_2006, wolfram_sociolinguistic_1969}
    \begin{itemize}
      \item[$\to$] African-American Language (AAL) becomes a monolith
    \end{itemize}
    \item Variation within marginalized groups \smallcite{jones_toward_2015, rahman_middle-class_2008, wolfram_american_2016} and social meaning brought into focus \smallcite{eberhardt_first_2015, reyes_appropriation_2005}
      \begin{itemize}
        \item[$\to$] The monolith is broken up but sociological concepts of race are still absent
      \end{itemize}
    \item Raciolinguistics aims to take a sociological view of race to sociolinguistics \smallcite{rosa_unsettling_2017}
  \end{enumerate}
\end{frame}